    {
      "number": 4,
      "id": "I_kwDOJ0geBc6FtAzt",
      "title": "Notepad for IETF 118",
      "url": "https://github.com/LucasWang86/fcbgp--framework/issues/4",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "BasilGuo",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "[Minutes IETF118: idr: Tue 12:00](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/minutes-118-idr-202311071200/)\r\n\r\n# Framework of Forwarding Commitment BGP (15 mins)\r\n\r\n> Keyur:\r\n>   1. As WG chair, suggest to present in SIDROPS also.\r\n>   2. As WG member, you may think about decentralize this to solve different kinds of dos attack.\r\n>   3. In term of scale and convergence performance, need to consider router's CPU are different from computer CPUs.\r\n>\r\n> Jeff:\r\n>   1. The procedure in the draft is incomplete. Need to talk more about what goes into the path attributes.\r\n>   2. This is close to SoBGP, while replay and spoofing could be easier.\r\n>\r\n> Zhuotao: For the replay attack, plan to add timestamp. And think with pathlet it still can secure the entire path.\r\n>\r\n> Jeff: Then it means you need to rely on the immediate upstream to tell you the truth.\r\n>\r\n> Andrew: As operator without AD hat, have great concern about RIR based route invalidation.\r\n>\r\n> Randy Bush: We are in the condition now with ROV, nobody complains about serious breakage.\r\n>\r\n> Andrew: It does not mean it will not happen. Take a look at the number of routes being signed in Africa and ask why.\r\n\r\nThough this draft is not presented at IETF 118, these questions/suggestions still apply to this draft.\r\n\r\nThe draft we present at IETF 118 is [draft-wang-idr-frameworkoffcbgp-00 - Framework of Forwarding Commitment BGP](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-wang-idr-frameworkoffcbgp/) and the Github repository link is [LucasWang86/framework-of-fcbgp](https://github.com/LucasWang86/framework-of-fcbgp/).\r\n\r\nIt seems no need to maintain so many repositories. I decided to merge these repositories. We'd better manage these repositories in one account/place, such as in [FCBGP](https://github.com/FCBGP) which maintains the I-D.FC-BGP Protocol Specification.",
      "createdAt": "2024-04-15T09:26:56Z",
      "updatedAt": "2024-04-15T09:26:56Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    }
